                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Lang : LocallyCartesianClosedCategories \to DependentTypeTheories
          %p
            from
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+categories"} locally cartesian closed categories
            to
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            that sends each category to its
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
          %p The important fact is that
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Lang
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lang
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p
            This is discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
          %p
            For the case of
            = succeed "/" do
